                "entry_id": "4a38b3b8-6751-3083-b4e7-71f3b127f379",
                "word": "opschroeven",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a733606d-fb1d-3b29-85c2-b4c7d9c1cfa0",
                        "entry_id": "4a38b3b8-6751-3083-b4e7-71f3b127f379",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iets groter of hoger maken, of dat alleen maar beloven"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "57732f48-d0e1-4f6a-99d6-fe63599ca872",
                                "sense_id": "a733606d-fb1d-3b29-85c2-b4c7d9c1cfa0",
                                "text": "Het opschroeven van de financiële ambities eind 2006 was het gevolg van druk van de ‘peer group’, zegt Bergen. Andere banken zoals Deutsche Bank haalden een hoger rendement, KBC moest hoger mikken. ‘Professionele beleggers vonden ons niet ambitieus genoeg. De sfeer was bijna van: hoe durf je hier binnenkomen om je aandeel aan te prijzen’, zegt Bergen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b83890f2-5686-4bb1-8b02-acefb4339484",
                                "sense_id": "a733606d-fb1d-3b29-85c2-b4c7d9c1cfa0",
                                "text": "Tesla kan productie Model 3 opschroeven na ophalen 1,8 miljard"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5717ce1d-2be8-44d1-b704-2b3aa8cb2a6f",
                                "sense_id": "a733606d-fb1d-3b29-85c2-b4c7d9c1cfa0",
                                "text": "Ik besloot mijn tempo op te schroeven, in de hoop andere hikers in te halen en me bij hen aan te sluiten."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0c507aeb-458e-41ee-b59c-2f0c632ffbb7",
                        "source_entry_id": "4a38b3b8-6751-3083-b4e7-71f3b127f379",
                        "source_sense_id": "a733606d-fb1d-3b29-85c2-b4c7d9c1cfa0",
                        "source_sense_description": "iets groter of hoger maken, of dat alleen maar beloven",
                        "target_lang_word": "exaggerate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "exaggerate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "387dda93-8642-3ade-a11b-3cbc5fbc2daa",
                                        "entry_id": "267d14e8-8410-3c40-8d7e-2a44f15953f3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To overstate, to describe more than the fact."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0cd03e83-7b33-4408-b8ea-b4fbb0a09fbb",
                                                "sense_id": "387dda93-8642-3ade-a11b-3cbc5fbc2daa",
                                                "text": "I've told you a billion times not to exaggerate!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4638d36b-a7ef-4e1a-aef2-97f3c8855e67",
                                                "sense_id": "387dda93-8642-3ade-a11b-3cbc5fbc2daa",
                                                "text": "He said he’d slept with hundreds of girls, but I know he’s exaggerating. The real number is about ten."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d6a8a4d-bf81-4636-908b-c9e4f814ebfb",
                                                "sense_id": "387dda93-8642-3ade-a11b-3cbc5fbc2daa",
                                                "text": "These testosterone thumpers have repackaged and exaggerated the study, with a credulity born of zealotry, into articles with shitposty titles like “Trust The Science: Study Links Left-Wing Politics to Lower Testosterone,” casting it as hard proof of their hormonal theories of healthy politics."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "exaggerate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b90be0fd-67c8-3fba-b524-8ba76098536b",
                                        "entry_id": "235b0f54-75db-3d5f-a652-c2e46c45efec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Exaggerative; overblown."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c9e7b34-b4e5-4fc7-adb9-ef660dbbefa3",
                                                "sense_id": "b90be0fd-67c8-3fba-b524-8ba76098536b",
                                                "text": "And in general, if it is a natural feeling, let it be, but at normal, living levels, not too exaggerate."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f6f6a5f-b68c-403b-ab93-734e03162ada",
                                                "sense_id": "b90be0fd-67c8-3fba-b524-8ba76098536b",
                                                "text": "Water was invading, like some loving arms, some protecting wings, but its love and care were too exaggerate, they were deadly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7827d7c-ea97-48d0-9057-f50aa0633d76",
                                                "sense_id": "b90be0fd-67c8-3fba-b524-8ba76098536b",
                                                "text": "You will leave [the camp] and when confronted to the smallest inconvenience you will have again these reactions that, for me, are very exaggerate."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19ac3d0e-d9bd-484a-b095-3878b36755a9",
                                                "sense_id": "b90be0fd-67c8-3fba-b524-8ba76098536b",
                                                "text": "From this comparison, it seems that the data in Table 7.7 are reasonable, while Ashbel's values are exaggerate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
